lestone":null,"comments":14,"created_at":"2024-03-17T10:02:56Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T08:36:20Z","closed_at":null,"author_association":"NONE","sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"active_lock_reason":null,"body":"### Is there an existing issue for this?

- [X] I have searched the existing issues

### Summary

**As a** user
**I want** to access request data
**So that I** may set environment variables globally based on data that exists in the request but does not exist in the response

E.g.:

Example pre request script

```js
pw.env.set("auth_user_password", pw.request.body.password); 
```

Example test script

```js
pw.test("Status code is 201", ()=> {
    const status = pw.response.status
    const data = pw.response.body

    pw.expect(status).toBe(201);
    pw.expect(typeof data.email).toBeType("string");
    pw.expect(typeof data.id).toBeType("string");

    pw.env.set("auth_user_password", pw.request.body.password); 
    pw.env.set("auth_user_email", data.email);
    pw.env.set("auth_user_id", data.id);
});
```

I would be willing to work on this, but I would need initial pointers.

### Why should this be worked on?

It's a nice feature available in both postman and insomnia. Currently, me and my team want to migrate away from Postman's aggressive price tag and we believe Hoppscotch has made great improvements in the last few months. We want to adopt Hoppscotch, but adopting it right now, means we don't have some "niceties" on scripted request we use often during development.

